  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening co-creation capacities for feminist and collaborative journalism</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Organization of a Mediat&#xf3;n, a space for journalistic exploration and innovation, as an innovative and collaborative strategy to strengthen our work with other media and civil society organizations, develop innovative journalistic products in a collaborative manner, and strengthen Alharaca&apos;s operational capacities.
The Mediat&#xf3;n will strengthen our internal capacities as an organization and at the same time foster collaboration and the exchange of ideas among diverse social actors committed to the defense of human rights and the promotion of a democratic culture in El Salvador. In addition, this initiative will contribute to the creation of innovative and quality journalistic content by Alharaca in alliance with other media and organizations. The theme of the Mediat&#xf3;n will be &#x201c;Community Voices&#x201d; to focus the content on amplifying the narratives and stories of those sectors of society that are often marginalized or ignored by traditional media such as women, LGBTIQA+ people, indigenous communities, land defenders, rural communities, among others. Therefore, the Mediat&#xf3;n represents an opportunity to enhance the impact and relevance of our journalistic work in an adverse and hostile context for women, the LGBTIQA+ community and freedom of press and expression.</narrative>
  </description>
